---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';
---

<BaseLayout title="Study Tips & Exam Guides for O & A-Levels | A-Worthy Blog" description="Free study tips, exam strategies and guides for O-Level English & Maths, H1 General Paper and H2 Economics from A-Worthy's SHARP Method tutors in Singapore." ogImage="/images/og-blog.png">
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="blog-head">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow" data-animate="reveal-up">Blog</span>
          <h1 class="page-title" data-animate="reveal-up">Study tips, exam strategies &amp; <span class="accent-word">guides</span></h1>
          <p class="page-subtitle" data-animate="reveal-up">Exam technique, revision plans and admissions guides for <span class="nobreak">O-Level</span> English &amp; Maths, H1 General Paper and H2 Economics, from A-Worthy.</p>
        </div>
        <img src="/images/mascots/mascot-reading.webp" alt="" width="477" height="640" class="blog-head__sticker sticker sticker--right" />
      </div>

      <div class="blog-grid" data-animate="reveal-up">
        <article class="blog-card blog-card--featured card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/choosing-jc-subject-combinations/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--gold">Admissions</span>
            <h2>Choosing Your JC Subject Combination: Rules, Prerequisites and Strategy</h2>
            <p>The contrasting-subject rule, the 70-point admission score, which university courses need which subjects, and how to choose a fourth subject. Sourced from MOE, NUS and NTU&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>23 September 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/sec-examination-guide/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--pink">For Parents</span>
            <h2>The SEC Examination from 2027: What Changes for Your Child</h2>
            <p>From 2027 the O-Level becomes the SEC, and JC admission moves from L1R5 &le; 20 to L1R4 &le; 16. What today&rsquo;s Sec 3 students need to know, from MOE and SEAB sources&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>23 September 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/ib-vs-jc/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--gold">Admissions</span>
            <h2>IB or JC? How to Choose the Right Path After O-Levels</h2>
            <p>The IB Diploma and the JC A-Levels side by side: curriculum, assessment, workload, university recognition, costs, and which suits your child&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>27 May 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/how-to-choose-a-tuition-centre-singapore/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--pink">For Parents</span>
            <h2>How to Choose a Tuition Centre in Singapore</h2>
            <p>Every centre says it has small classes and proven results. The seven things that actually tell them apart, and the red flags that should make you walk away&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta"><span>27 May 2026</span></div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/does-my-child-need-tuition/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--pink">For Parents</span>
            <h2>Does My Child Actually Need Tuition?</h2>
            <p>Tuition is a tool, not a rite of passage. The signs that it will help your child, and the problems it won&rsquo;t fix&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta"><span>27 May 2026</span></div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/a-maths-calculus-guide/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--green">O-Level Mathematics</span>
            <h2>A-Maths Calculus Made Simple: Differentiation &amp; Integration</h2>
            <p>Calculus makes a lot of A-Maths students nervous, but once you know the rules it&rsquo;s one of the most predictable topics. What differentiation and integration do, where the marks are, and the traps to avoid&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>27 May 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/e-maths-vs-a-maths/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--green">O-Level Mathematics</span>
            <h2>E-Maths vs A-Maths: What&rsquo;s the Difference &mdash; and Should Your Child Take A-Maths?</h2>
            <p>A subject choice that confuses a lot of families. What each covers, how they&rsquo;re assessed, why A-Maths is taken <em>in addition</em> to E-Maths, and how to decide&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>27 May 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/o-level-maths-common-mistakes/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--green">O-Level Mathematics</span>
            <h2>7 Careless Mistakes That Cost O-Level Maths Marks</h2>
            <p>Plenty of O-Level Maths marks are lost to method, not knowledge: the wrong approach, skipped working, early rounding. The 7 careless mistakes we see most often, and the SHARP fix for each&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>27 May 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/o-level-cut-off-points/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--gold">O-Level Admissions</span>
            <h2>2026 O-Level Cut-Off Points for JC: The Complete L1R5 Guide</h2>
            <p>Full 2026 JAE cut-off points for every Singapore JC, ranked by L1R5. How the aggregate is calculated, bonus points, and the two subjects that shift your score the most&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>26 May 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/o-level-english-tips/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--blue">O-Level English</span>
            <h2>10 O-Level English Tips to Score A1</h2>
            <p>An A1 comes from knowing exactly what the examiner wants. Ten tips across Paper 1 and Paper 2, from the STAMP CARD editing sweep to timing each question by its marks&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>15 May 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/gp-essay-examples/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--gold">H1 General Paper</span>
            <h2>GP Essay Examples: 5 Model Introductions That Score</h2>
            <p>Your introduction sets the tone for the whole GP essay. 5 model introductions on Technology, Environment, Media, Globalisation and Arts, each with the technique it uses and why it earns Band 3 marks&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>10 May 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/h2-econs-case-study-tips/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--pink">H2 Economics</span>
            <h2>H2 Economics Case Study: How to Score L3 Every Time</h2>
            <p>Case study answers often lose marks on the extracts and on evaluation. A step-by-step guide to reading the extracts, using the data, bringing in diagrams and writing the evaluation that reaches L3, with a worked example&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>8 May 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/comprehension-techniques/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--blue">O-Level English</span>
            <h2>10 Comprehension Techniques That Top Students Use</h2>
            <p>Many comprehension marks are lost by misreading what the question asks. 10 techniques from the SHARP Method for working out what each question type wants&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>25 Mar 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/gp-essay-structure/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--gold">H1 General Paper</span>
            <h2>How to Structure a GP Essay for Band 3 and Above</h2>
            <p>Structure, more than knowledge, separates a Band 2 GP essay from a Band 3 one. We walk one essay question through SHARP, using P-E-E-L paragraphs to turn scattered arguments into an essay the examiner can follow&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>18 Mar 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/economics-essay-diagrams/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--pink">H2 Economics</span>
            <h2>The Complete Guide to Economics Essay Diagrams</h2>
            <p>In an H2 Economics essay, a clean, correctly labelled diagram shows the examiner you know the model. The diagrams you need, from market failure to exchange rates, with step-by-step drawing instructions&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>11 Mar 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/why-smart-students-fail/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--green">Study Tips</span>
            <h2>Why Smart Students Still Fail &mdash; And How to Fix It</h2>
            <p>They understand the content and can explain it out loud. Then the exam paper lands and they freeze. Why that gap between knowing and scoring opens up, and how to close it&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>4 Mar 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/situational-writing-guide/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--blue">O-Level English</span>
            <h2>O-Level Situational Writing: Marks, Planning and Format</h2>
            <p>How the 30 marks split between Task Fulfilment and Language, the PAC analysis, the four-move expansion for every point, and the format for all seven text types&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>25 Feb 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="blog-card card-lift">
          <a href="/blog/exam-prep-timeline/" class="blog-card-link">
            <span class="blog-tag chip chip--blue">Exam Strategy</span>
            <h2>The 3-Month Exam Prep Timeline That Actually Works</h2>
            <p>With 12 weeks to the O-Levels or A-Levels, many students panic and try to revise everything at once. A week-by-week plan, from content review to full papers under exam conditions&hellip;</p>
            <div class="blog-meta">
              <span>18 Feb 2026</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="blog-subscribe" data-animate="reveal-up">
        <h3>Get new articles by email</h3>
        <p>Leave your email and we&rsquo;ll send you each new article when it goes up.</p>
        <form class="subscribe-form" id="blog-subscribe-form" novalidate>
          <input type="email" id="blog-subscribe-email" placeholder="Your email address" aria-label="Email address" required autocomplete="email" />
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-accent">Subscribe</button>
        </form>
        <p class="subscribe-msg" id="blog-subscribe-msg" role="status" hidden></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    function initBlogSub() {
      var form = document.getElementById('blog-subscribe-form');
      if (!form) return;
      var input = document.getElementById('blog-subscribe-email');
      var msg = document.getElementById('blog-subscribe-msg');
      var btn = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
      form.onsubmit = function (e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        var email = ((input && input.value) || '').trim();
        msg.classList.remove('subscribe-msg--error');
        if (!email || !/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(email)) {
          msg.textContent = 'Please enter a valid email address.';
          msg.classList.add('subscribe-msg--error');
          msg.hidden = false;
          if (input) input.focus();
          return;
        }
        if (btn) { btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = 'Subscribing…'; }
        fetch('https://formspree.io/f/xreoozkk', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Accept': 'application/json', 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify({ email: email, _subject: 'Blog newsletter subscription' })
        }).then(function (res) {
          if (!res.ok) throw new Error('failed');
          form.reset();
          form.hidden = true;
          msg.textContent = 'Thanks, you’re subscribed. We’ll email you when the next article goes up.';
          msg.hidden = false;
          if (window.plausible) window.plausible('Newsletter Signup');
          if (window.aworthyCelebrate) window.aworthyCelebrate();
        }).catch(function () {
          msg.textContent = 'Something went wrong. Please try again, or message us on WhatsApp.';
          msg.classList.add('subscribe-msg--error');
          msg.hidden = false;
          if (btn) { btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = 'Subscribe'; }
        });
      };
    }
    initBlogSub();
  })();
</script>

<style>
  .blog-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .blog-head__sticker {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 150px;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .blog-head__sticker { display: none; }
  }
  .page-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.5vw, 3.8rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.08;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .page-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    /* rem, not px: 640px at the 16px root (unchanged ≤1440) and it grows with the
       root font above 1440, so the subtitle keeps ~67 characters per line instead
       of breaking into three 44-character lines at 2560. */
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  /* From 1024px up the subtitle line broke at the hyphen ("excel in O-" / "Level") */
  .nobreak { white-space: nowrap; }
  .blog-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }
  /* Article cards — white ink stickers; hover lift comes from the global .card-lift */
  .blog-card {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .blog-card-link {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    height: 100%;
  }
  .blog-card--featured {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    max-width: 100%;
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .blog-tag {
    align-self: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }
  .blog-card h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .blog-card--featured h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .blog-card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }
  /* The featured card spans the whole grid: without a cap its excerpt ran ~150
     characters on a single line from 1280px up. */
  .blog-card--featured p { max-width: 68ch; }
  .blog-meta {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 2px dashed var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }
  .blog-subscribe {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 2px solid var(--color-ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    box-shadow: 0 3px 0 var(--ink-shadow);
    padding: 3rem;
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .blog-subscribe h3 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .blog-subscribe p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .subscribe-form {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 400px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .subscribe-form input {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .subscribe-msg {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--tint-green-fg);
  }
  .subscribe-msg--error {
    color: var(--color-accent-text);
  }
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .blog-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
  /* Two-column range (tablets): the featured card fills row 1, so an odd number of
     regular cards left the last one alone beside an empty slot. Let that lone last
     card span the row (it only matches when it really is alone: an even child index). */
  @media (min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px) {
    .blog-card:last-child:nth-child(even) { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .blog-card:last-child:nth-child(even) p { max-width: 68ch; }
  }
  /* Laptops/desktops: card excerpts and the subscribe blurb were 14.4px */
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .blog-card p,
    .blog-subscribe p { font-size: 0.95rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .blog-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .blog-card { padding: 1.5rem; }
    .blog-card--featured {
      grid-column: 1;
    }
    .blog-subscribe { padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .subscribe-form {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
